  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Women and historical memory in El Salvador</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project aims to assist in strengthening grassroots organisations&#x2019; capacity to analyse and understand women&#x2019;s roles in history, in El Salvador.

Whilst levels of community organisation in El Salvador and throughout Central America are relatively good, grassroots sectors of civil society are often lacking basic information, analysis and understanding about the economic and political systems, structures and trends that shape their reality and impact their lives and livelihoods. There are very few spaces for systematic training of grassroots and community leaders and educators (agents of change) in education, (particularly gender) analysis and reflection. There is a scarcity of publishing houses dedicated to producing quality, user friendly educational support materials on social, economic, political and environmental development issues for these popular sectors. 

Equipo Ma&#xed;z is dedicated to popular education through publications and training and aims to facilitate learning and analysis at the grassroots on issues that affect local people, to enable them to have a better understanding of these issues and the capacity to propose alternative policies and solutions. It aims to increase people&#x2019;s commitment to social justice and encourages them to take an active role in creating change.   

Through this project, Equipo Maiz is part of the new CAFOD Regional Gender and HIV Capacity strengthening Programme and the Human Rights and Governance programme. This year will be dedicated to working with women and men from grassroots organisations to strengthen their analysis capacity to understand women&apos;s role in history and to plan activities from a historical and gender equity perspective. Last year of funding: Phasing out.</narrative>
  </description>
